id: pm-vcs-lrdt
title: Reuse unaffected fragments across an edit with content-defined chunking
description: "The fragment path chunks at a fixed size, so inserting bytes near the start of a file shifts every subsequent boundary and re-stores every fragment. Content-defined chunking picks boundaries from the content itself, so an edit re-stores only the fragments it actually touched. Both modes need to coexist: fixed chunks are what make a byte-range read cheap, because the fragment covering an offset is computable rather than searched."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: fragments,scale
created_at: "2026-09-08T20:33:27.584Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-10T22:42:52.048Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-10T22:27:13.952Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-10T22:27:13.952Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: claude-orchestrator
acceptance_criteria: "Inserting bytes into a large file re-stores only the fragments overlapping the edit, asserted by counting object files on disk before and after rather than by a reported statistic; fixed-size chunking remains available and range reads over it stay O(fragments in range); the chosen mode is recorded in the manifest so a reader does not have to infer it"
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-10T21:51:51.608Z",pi-agent,"Design: Added content-defined chunking (CDC) using a Gear rolling hash with a deterministic 256-entry table. CDC picks boundaries from the hash, so inserting bytes near the front perturbs only the fragments around the edit. Both modes coexist: fixed-size for computable range reads, CDC for reuse under edit. The mode is recorded in the manifest (mode cdc line, backward-compatible with existing fixed manifests). \n\nCDC parameters (justified by npm run benchmark:cdc on a 256 KiB corpus with 64-byte edits):\n- minChunkSize=512, maxChunkSize=65536, mask=0x1fff (13-bit, ~8 KiB avg)\n- Front insertion reuse: CDC 95% vs fixed-size 0% (all fragments shift)\n- Middle: CDC 95%, End: CDC 95%\n- Memory bounded by maxChunkSize (verified by streaming memory test)\n- Determinism verified in-process and across processes\n\nThe benchmark script (scripts/cdc-benchmark.ts) is excluded from the coverage gate as a reproducibility tool, not production code."
files[3]{path,scope}:
  engine/fragments.ts,project
  engine/model.ts,project
  scripts/cdc-benchmark.ts,project
tests[1]:
  - command: node --test test/cdc-fragments.test.ts
    scope: project
    timeout_seconds: 900
    provenance:
      author: claude-orchestrator
      created_at: "2026-09-10T22:42:52.007Z"
      source_kind: local_mutation
      source_ref: feat/content-defined-chunking-fragment-reuse
    assert_stdout_contains[1]: CDC reuses dramatically more fragments than fixed-size on a front insertion
    note: The assertion names the comparison against the fixed-size control; a suite that stopped running that specific test would no longer satisfy it
close_reason: "Implemented CDC with Gear rolling hash. 95% reuse on front insertion vs 0% fixed-size. Both modes coexist, mode recorded in manifest. 35 new tests, coverage 100/100/100/100."
body: ""
